================================================================
TOP-SEVERITY FINDS
================================================================

[CRITICAL] a2015829 fix(recorder): persist ended_at after import event loop
  src/core/recorder.rs:2074-2150. `execute_recorder_import` inserted the
  `recorder_runs` row with ended_at=None (required because events have FK
  into the run), computed ended_at after the event loop, stamped it into
  the API response, returned — but never updated the DB row.
  - API contract said RFC3339 timestamp; DB stayed NULL forever.
  - Broke `ee recorder list --completed-only`, every audit/forensics
    join on ended_at, and downstream `audit_log_recorder_run_ended`
    lookups.
  - Latent data-API divergence — surfaces only in production when a
    consumer joins or filters on ended_at and silently misses every
    imported run.

[HIGH] 294dc1e7 fix(serve): close bearer-token timing side channel in serve_auth_state
  src/serve.rs:670. `serve_auth_state` compared inbound Authorization
  header to configured token via `value == &format!("Bearer {token}")`.
  String `==` delegates to short-circuit memcmp.
  - With `MIN_SERVE_TOKEN_BITS = 256` an attacker measuring HTTP
    response latency could recover the EE_SERVE_TOKEN byte-by-byte
    via standard timing analysis.
  - Replaced with constant-time compare.

[HIGH] 43ebe03b fix(focus_suggest): defend recent_hours from DateTime overflow
  src/core/focus_suggest.rs:128-159. `--recent-hours u32::MAX` panicked
  the CLI: `recent_hours: u32` accepts up to ~489_957 years; chrono's
  `DateTime<Utc>` is bounded to ±262_143 years; `Utc::now() -
  Duration::hours(...)` overflowed chrono's representable range and
  panicked.
  - Benign-looking flag value → local CLI denial-of-service.
  - Fix uses checked_sub_signed + DateTime::MIN_UTC fallback +
    new recent_hours_window_clamped degraded code + E2E pinning the
    regression with --recent-hours 4294967295.

[HIGH (cross-platform reliability)] edd17760 fix(init): cross-platform RawMode coercion
  src/core/init.rs:672-689. cod_3's bd-l9e9i fix + my bd-1idcb carry-over
  hardcoded a u16 conversion before `rustix::fs::Mode::from_raw_mode`. But
  `RawMode` is platform-aliased:
  - Linux (linux_raw + libc/glibc backends): RawMode = ffi::c_uint (u32)
  - macOS / BSDs (libc backend): RawMode = c::mode_t (u16)
  Local Mac build was green; canonical Linux checkout at
  /data/projects/eidetic_engine_cli would have failed to compile. Caught
  by p1 in Round 1 fresh-eyes review of just-shipped peer commits.

================================================================
PATTERN HIGHLIGHTS
================================================================

By the numbers — distinct defect classes the review phase hardened:

  Bounded-allocation defense (caps on fs::read*):
    ~32 distinct file paths. Every peer-modifiable workspace file
    now has an explicit size guard ahead of the read, preventing
    pre-sized allocation attacks (`fs::read_to_string` pre-sizes
    from metadata length on all supported platforms).
  TOCTOU closes (O_NOFOLLOW + open-fd patterns):
    ~10 paths. Hook files, init permissions, artifact reads, cache
    set_permissions via fchmod through open fd, backup hash check
    + read on undo, etc.
  HTTP parser hardening (RFC 7230):
    ee serve's request-line parser tightened to RFC-compliant
    single-SP-only; Transfer-Encoding rejects chunked-in-list +
    chunked-with-parameters; bearer-token compare made
    constant-time.
  Determinism (total_cmp on float sort surfaces):
    ee.why.influence.v1, ee.why.loadBearing, insights
    causalBottlenecks + hits + proximityHotspots, pack omissions,
    memory dedupe-check warnings. NaN-safe total ordering applied
    everywhere.
  Cross-platform reliability:
    rustix Mode coercion (u16/u32 platform-aliased), curl wrapper
    --connect-timeout + --max-time defaults, Linux/Mac/BSD
    permission semantics matched.
  Schema/contract drift:
    severity drift on shared codes (cass_unavailable,
    graph_unavailable) aligned to canonical fixtures;
    focus_suggest empty-spanIds violation of minLength:1 closed;
    recorder ended_at API/DB divergence (the CRITICAL).
  Resource cleanup:
    hooks temp-file orphan on write/sync/rename failure; doctor
    backup undo TOCTOU; recovery-state.json size guards.

